# The search ability costs {1} besides tapping and sacrificing the Vein, and the Vein's own mana cannot pay it (its tap is part of the cost): alone on turn 1 it is not
# offered (the refusal; the next scenario, with an Island beside it, is the positive control). On turn 3, with an Island, Bot1 searches a library that holds no basic land
# card - only Karakas - and finds nothing: the Vein is still sacrificed, the Island stays, and no land arrives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Promising Vein
Island
Island x5
Island
Karakas x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Promising Vein.Play
! Bot1.Battlefield.Promising Vein.Activate(Ability: Search; Mana: short)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Promising Vein.Activate(Ability: Search)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Search()

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Promising Vein
